1
00:00:18,188 --> 00:00:32,834
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,938 --> 00:02:08,868
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

3
00:02:17,251 --> 00:02:21,701
Osman Bey, do you have time?
We couldn't talk.

4
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:44,370
Not now, Malhun Hatun.
Not now.

5
00:02:46,711 --> 00:02:49,761
Alps!

6
00:03:11,619 --> 00:03:14,979
To the potter.

7
00:03:46,281 --> 00:03:48,841
Osman?

8
00:04:19,803 --> 00:04:24,353
Osman Bey, spare my life!

9
00:04:25,718 --> 00:04:28,848
Spare my life, Osman Bey!

10
00:04:29,413 --> 00:04:36,063
If I take your life, it would be blessing.

11
00:04:38,001 --> 00:04:42,001
Who are you working for? Who?

12
00:04:43,137 --> 00:04:48,407
Who is holding your leashes?
Tell me! Who?

13
00:04:48,631 --> 00:04:53,921
I will tell you. I will.
I will tell you everything!

14
00:04:54,976 --> 00:05:00,266
The traitors are your closest ones,
Osman Bey.

15
00:05:01,916 --> 00:05:05,106
Who?

16
00:05:05,679 --> 00:05:09,679
-Who is that?
-The traitor is--

17
00:05:34,771 --> 00:05:39,691
The arrow came this way.
Come on, alps!

18
00:06:19,052 --> 00:06:23,952
Boran, go this way.
Bala...

19
00:06:27,542 --> 00:06:32,102
-You stay here.
-As you order, my bey.

20
00:06:41,888 --> 00:06:45,888
The arrow came from here, it seems.

21
00:06:47,794 --> 00:06:53,624
-How can you be so sure?
-I saw a shadow on the window.

22
00:06:53,624 --> 00:06:56,614
And the footprints prove me.
He was here.

23
00:07:26,753 --> 00:07:33,183
-Who are you?
-Your death, Osman. Your death!

24
00:07:36,223 --> 00:07:39,673
I'm here, Osman Bey!

25
00:07:43,157 --> 00:07:48,237
-Where did you come from, nephew?
-From now, I'll always be with you!

26
00:07:50,278 --> 00:07:55,188
Then, show me your valiance!

27
00:08:28,456 --> 00:08:32,456
Come on, to the horses.

28
00:08:39,939 --> 00:08:42,889
Give me the bow.

29
00:08:46,698 --> 00:08:49,498
Come on, my lion!

30
00:09:15,585 --> 00:09:23,055
My bey killed them all. Let us check
around. It's good to be cautious.

31
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:28,840
Gencebay, hold, brother.

32
00:09:31,755 --> 00:09:35,708
Let us check them good.

33
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:40,858
They wore like kayı people but
there must be something else.

34
00:09:40,858 --> 00:09:43,688
Come on, brother.
Come on.

35
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:17,596
We are looking but do we know what
we are looking for? No need to waste time.

36
00:10:17,964 --> 00:10:23,034
We don't know, brother. We don't.
But it's good to be cautious.

37
00:10:51,169 --> 00:10:53,889
Brother.

38
00:10:57,612 --> 00:11:00,912
What is that?

39
00:11:15,914 --> 00:11:20,904
If they are doing this in Söğüt
in the sun light...

40
00:11:20,904 --> 00:11:24,904
...Osman Bey must have many enemies.

41
00:11:27,876 --> 00:11:31,876
What's happening, Bala Hatun?

42
00:11:37,658 --> 00:11:41,658
What's cooking here?

43
00:11:41,658 --> 00:11:45,658
What is? Thank Allah, Osman Bey
can stop everyone's plans.

44
00:11:46,745 --> 00:11:51,825
If Osman Bey will struggle with every
problem, why are you here, Bala Hatun?

45
00:11:54,432 --> 00:11:59,952
I'm won't take lessons from you on
how to help my husband. Know your place!

46
00:12:00,277 --> 00:12:07,357
I'm Umur Bey's daughter! I know my place
and what to say to anyone!

47
00:12:07,357 --> 00:12:12,557
-Good.
-But it's not the time to speak.

48
00:12:12,557 --> 00:12:16,197
It's time to work.

49
00:12:19,879 --> 00:12:23,879
-Let's leave here.
-Let's go.

50
00:13:52,006 --> 00:13:55,396
Ya Allah!

51
00:15:14,523 --> 00:15:18,523
Who is this traitor, my bey?
Do you know him?

52
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:29,215
I don't know him, Bayhoca.

53
00:15:40,749 --> 00:15:45,849
My nephew, I see that you leave
no burden to me.

54
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:54,932
You are fighting for the Muslim Turks,
carrying their burden, my bey.

55
00:15:55,922 --> 00:15:59,922
Let us handle such small things.

56
00:16:00,305 --> 00:16:05,245
My nephew, this is the path of jihad.

57
00:16:06,002 --> 00:16:12,870
The one who carries the flag of Islam...

58
00:16:12,870 --> 00:16:19,910
...is one with the one who cries
Allah's name in the field.

59
00:16:20,464 --> 00:16:27,114
May you live long, my bey. You lead us
so we can subjugate the great mountains.

60
00:16:27,353 --> 00:16:31,843
You ask for jihad, so we can destroy
the heathens.

61
00:16:32,021 --> 00:16:36,731
You give the order and we will do it,
my bey.

62
00:16:41,511 --> 00:16:47,691
Thank you, nephew.
Thank you. May you live long.

63
00:16:48,444 --> 00:16:54,504
A Kayı warrior should speak like this.

64
00:17:53,334 --> 00:17:55,864
My bey...

65
00:17:56,616 --> 00:17:58,906
My bey?

66
00:18:00,126 --> 00:18:04,126
The heathen is uncircumcised.

67
00:18:10,475 --> 00:18:14,795
We'll find out who he is.

68
00:18:26,068 --> 00:18:31,068
Who are you?
Who are you, I say!

69
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:35,819
Who are you?
Who are you?

70
00:19:02,272 --> 00:19:07,052
-Where are you taking me?
-To your salvation, Dündar Bey.

71
00:19:27,494 --> 00:19:33,054
-Who are you? Who are you?
-That's not the time, Dündar Bey.

72
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:43,650
Who are you serving for?
Who are you? Who are you?

73
00:20:10,488 --> 00:20:14,488
Süleyman?

74
00:20:35,445 --> 00:20:38,725
Bala Hatun!

75
00:20:45,776 --> 00:20:50,616
-Who was the man Osman Bey caught?
-İdris.

76
00:20:52,154 --> 00:20:56,154
He was a potter.

77
00:20:59,804 --> 00:21:04,974
-What did he want from him?
-The price of treason.

78
00:21:06,269 --> 00:21:10,819
So the traitors entered into
your tribe?

79
00:21:15,379 --> 00:21:18,149
Bala.

80
00:21:19,756 --> 00:21:23,056
Malhun Hatun.

81
00:21:26,743 --> 00:21:30,743
What happened, my bey?
Have you caught the traitor?

82
00:21:30,743 --> 00:21:33,513
We have.

83
00:21:36,221 --> 00:21:40,221
We have but...

84
00:21:40,221 --> 00:21:44,221
...we still have suspicions.

85
00:21:47,149 --> 00:21:51,149
We followed the tracks.

86
00:21:52,906 --> 00:21:58,286
It seems that the tracks won't
lead us to anywhere.

87
00:22:03,660 --> 00:22:07,660
Malhun Hatun.

88
00:22:09,049 --> 00:22:13,969
Tell me, is there anything we
are missing?

89
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:26,280
No, Osman Bey.
I wonder what you think.

90
00:22:30,613 --> 00:22:34,613
I only think of questions.

91
00:22:40,681 --> 00:22:45,341
The answers are on the corpse
of the potter.

92
00:22:45,341 --> 00:22:50,081
Bala, go to the tribe with
Malhun Hatun.

93
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:56,620
As you want, my bey.

94
00:23:20,178 --> 00:23:25,508
I don't know who are you or
who are you serving for...

95
00:23:25,508 --> 00:23:31,848
...but don't forget that
I'm Osman Bey's uncle...

96
00:23:31,848 --> 00:23:36,398
...a Kayı bey,
Dündar!

97
00:23:38,027 --> 00:23:40,607
Never!

98
00:23:40,607 --> 00:23:45,227
Did you forget that we saved you
from Osman Bey's wrath?

99
00:23:45,955 --> 00:23:52,455
It seems that I saved you from
İdris' confession.

100
00:23:52,455 --> 00:23:59,765
You are a smart man, Dündar Bey.
We both should be thankful.

101
00:23:59,765 --> 00:24:05,365
We want nothing but your
good.

102
00:24:07,392 --> 00:24:13,202
You helped us a lot by letting
the Cumans enter the tribe.

103
00:24:14,652 --> 00:24:19,602
So, you are serving Nikola?

104
00:24:21,069 --> 00:24:27,389
We serve no one but our
lord and savior Jesus Christ!

105
00:24:29,641 --> 00:24:33,639
I believe that we have the same
interests...

106
00:24:33,639 --> 00:24:38,289
...as much as I believe in Jesus Christ,
Dündar Bey.

107
00:24:40,407 --> 00:24:44,307
What is there that I want but can't
take...

108
00:24:44,307 --> 00:24:47,777
...that you will give it to me?

109
00:24:47,777 --> 00:24:55,837
Just like Lord Nikola wants, we want you
to have what's your right, Dündar Bey.

110
00:24:58,044 --> 00:25:01,164
The beylig.

111
00:25:02,686 --> 00:25:06,686
The beylig?

112
00:25:09,477 --> 00:25:13,667
You want me to betray, like Nikola.

113
00:25:13,667 --> 00:25:17,874
And you say that you will make me
the bey in return.

114
00:25:18,812 --> 00:25:22,812
What will happen if I refuse?

115
00:25:23,913 --> 00:25:28,143
Will you kill a Kayı bey?

116
00:25:28,143 --> 00:25:31,713
Of course, no.

117
00:25:33,255 --> 00:25:37,945
But we can't stop your nephew
from killing you...

118
00:25:37,945 --> 00:25:43,375
...after finding out that you work with
Nikola and killed İdris the Potter.

119
00:25:46,859 --> 00:25:52,319
If I die, you won't get what you want.

120
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:32,630
This is the arrow of the traitor
we chased.

121
00:26:39,260 --> 00:26:43,520
Whoever killed the potter...

122
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:48,249
...he isn't the man we chased.

123
00:26:53,094 --> 00:26:57,984
Then, they mislead us.

124
00:27:01,854 --> 00:27:05,854
It's obvious that someone is
playing with us.

125
00:27:10,864 --> 00:27:15,714
My bey, we found this on one of
the traitors who stopped you.

126
00:27:29,125 --> 00:27:33,125
Who are they, Osman Bey?

127
00:27:40,030 --> 00:27:46,250
Whoever the snake is,
if they entered our tribe...

128
00:27:46,522 --> 00:27:51,042
...there is no need to search for
it far away.

129
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:57,772
-What's your order, my bey?
-Search the potter's tent and shop.

130
00:27:57,772 --> 00:28:00,192
-All right, my bey.
-All right, my bey.

131
00:28:00,192 --> 00:28:03,532
Send the alps to take the corpse.

132
00:28:34,055 --> 00:28:39,965
Do you think he will do what
we want?

133
00:28:41,063 --> 00:28:46,283
When he has Osman's bowstring
on his neck...

134
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:51,853
It's time to take care of Malhun and
her father Umur Bey.

135
00:28:52,157 --> 00:28:57,857
Umur Bey accepts Osman Bey's
invitation to settle in these lands...

136
00:28:57,857 --> 00:29:02,767
...this can turn into a barbarian invasion
on Bithynia.

137
00:29:02,767 --> 00:29:09,657
Because Umur Bey is one of the most
renowned Turkmen beys in Anatolia.

138
00:29:09,776 --> 00:29:14,616
Many other beys will follow him.

139
00:29:14,812 --> 00:29:18,812
Then, Osman will leave the fur
of the bey...

140
00:29:18,825 --> 00:29:23,315
...and sit on the throne of the sultan.

141
00:29:24,269 --> 00:29:30,139
Nikola has no plans against
Osman's plan.

142
00:29:30,139 --> 00:29:36,119
He still believes that he'll
ambush and kill Osman.

143
00:29:36,747 --> 00:29:42,857
That's why we are here, brother.
These lands are sacred...

144
00:29:43,398 --> 00:29:50,578
...too sacred to leave to Nikola's hands.

145
00:29:51,437 --> 00:29:55,897
So, what will we do?

146
00:29:56,945 --> 00:30:03,765
We'll work with the devil even
to stop Osman's invasion of Bithynia.

147
00:30:06,565 --> 00:30:11,265
First, we'll take care of Umur.

148
00:30:11,343 --> 00:30:16,063
His tribe has more population
than Osman's.

149
00:30:16,063 --> 00:30:20,853
Osman has 500 soldiers,
Umur Bey has 1000.

150
00:30:20,853 --> 00:30:24,553
You understand what does it mean,
right?

151
00:30:24,553 --> 00:30:30,313
-What's on your mind?
-Geyhatu's hunting dog Toygar.

152
00:30:30,690 --> 00:30:36,440
First, we'll help Toygar to
capture Umur Bey.

153
00:30:36,688 --> 00:30:43,208
Then, we'll unleash Toygar upon
Osman.

154
00:30:55,711 --> 00:31:00,381
This trip to Constantinople is
giving you stress, Nikola.

155
00:31:01,619 --> 00:31:06,589
It must be easy for someone who
doesn't know the weight of this crown.

156
00:31:20,177 --> 00:31:24,987
I don't like uninvited guests.

157
00:31:26,370 --> 00:31:31,170
Especially if the uninvited guest
is good for nothing.

158
00:31:34,708 --> 00:31:39,368
You won't think that way when
you hear why I came.

159
00:31:39,655 --> 00:31:43,655
Let me tell you why you came, Göktuğ.

160
00:31:43,655 --> 00:31:47,655
Maybe it's to tell me how you
failed in the raid?

161
00:31:49,188 --> 00:31:54,078
Or maybe it's to tell me how you
still serving Osman?

162
00:31:54,078 --> 00:31:59,818
If so, don't bother.
Because I have no doubts.

163
00:32:22,454 --> 00:32:26,904
Maybe this will help.

164
00:32:27,094 --> 00:32:32,274
-What's this?
-Osman Bey's settling plans.

165
00:32:44,271 --> 00:32:47,311
Where did you find them?

166
00:32:47,311 --> 00:32:52,271
While we were leaving the tribe,
I managed to hide them from Osman.

167
00:33:08,860 --> 00:33:13,700
So, you have the rest, you say?

168
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:18,970
Yes. But if you want to have them...

169
00:33:18,970 --> 00:33:22,970
...you should pay a price.

170
00:33:25,538 --> 00:33:30,448
I'm ready to pay you the price
with gold.

171
00:33:30,932 --> 00:33:36,212
But if these documents are fake,
Göktuğ...

172
00:33:36,549 --> 00:33:41,399
...then you'll pay very bad.

173
00:33:41,418 --> 00:33:48,098
And I will make you pay that price
when I return from Constantinople.

174
00:33:54,146 --> 00:33:59,166
Flatyos, remind me that.

175
00:34:00,003 --> 00:34:03,663
With great pleasure, Nikola.

176
00:34:15,879 --> 00:34:22,809
Until we find out if the documents
are fake, you'll be our guest, Göktuğ.

177
00:34:23,891 --> 00:34:27,891
I like caution.

178
00:34:30,758 --> 00:34:35,918
Flatyos, let us host our guest in
our dungeon.

179
00:34:45,681 --> 00:34:49,681
Believe me, I won't stay there for long.

180
00:34:51,836 --> 00:34:55,836
You will see that the documents
are real.

181
00:35:44,986 --> 00:35:51,076
Will you accompany him when
Nikola goes to Constantinople?

182
00:35:51,952 --> 00:35:55,952
It's none of your business.

183
00:36:19,432 --> 00:36:23,432
We searched İdris' tent, Osman Bey.

184
00:36:23,993 --> 00:36:27,993
We found nothing about his treachery.

185
00:36:27,993 --> 00:36:32,693
-May I enter, Osman Bey.
-Come.

186
00:36:40,813 --> 00:36:47,323
Osman Bey, these are İdris' personal
belongings from his store.

187
00:37:59,928 --> 00:38:05,388
Despite how much a man
wants to hide his religion...

188
00:38:05,724 --> 00:38:12,844
...he will still want to carry a sign
somewhere.

189
00:38:13,664 --> 00:38:18,864
To return to himself when
he is alone.

190
00:38:21,945 --> 00:38:27,235
Oh, Osman Bey, oh.
Who would believe that?

191
00:38:27,864 --> 00:38:34,604
He hid it from me even.
Oh, İdris, oh...

192
00:38:35,962 --> 00:38:40,822
Abdurrahman Ghazi, Bamsı Bey...

193
00:38:40,822 --> 00:38:45,682
...you fought with many heathens
alongside my father.

194
00:38:46,316 --> 00:38:49,116
Tell me.

195
00:38:53,020 --> 00:38:57,020
Who are they?

196
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:13,360
Abdurrahman Ghazi.

197
00:39:17,642 --> 00:39:21,642
They are the greatest of the heathens,
Osman Bey.

198
00:39:21,642 --> 00:39:26,242
The servants of the pope
carry this sign.

199
00:39:28,557 --> 00:39:33,637
Then, we'll find out...

200
00:39:33,637 --> 00:39:39,577
...if it was the pope's spies or someone
from the tribe who killed İdris.

201
00:39:40,573 --> 00:39:46,473
May Allah forbid, do you still think that
we have traitors among us?

202
00:39:46,473 --> 00:39:52,323
Inside or outside, we are running
out of time.

203
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:03,160
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come!

204
00:40:15,264 --> 00:40:19,264
Where are you coming from, uncle?

205
00:40:21,092 --> 00:40:25,092
I was at Söğüt, Osman Bey.

206
00:40:25,208 --> 00:40:28,508
What were you doing at Söğüt?

207
00:40:31,974 --> 00:40:35,624
It was about trade.

208
00:40:36,299 --> 00:40:39,829
I was following your orders, my bey.

209
00:40:39,829 --> 00:40:42,589
Is that so?

210
00:40:43,927 --> 00:40:47,927
Were you preparing a new caravan?

211
00:40:52,347 --> 00:40:58,537
Will this be like the last one?

212
00:41:00,311 --> 00:41:06,931
My bey, who would've thought
of putting someone in the caravan?

213
00:41:06,931 --> 00:41:10,931
Someone have.

214
00:41:16,066 --> 00:41:20,996
-How did they know?
-May I enter, my bey?

215
00:41:23,336 --> 00:41:26,426
Come.

216
00:41:30,832 --> 00:41:34,622
News, my bey.

217
00:42:04,977 --> 00:42:09,907
This is the situation...

218
00:42:13,807 --> 00:42:20,647
...I witnessed a murder and found
evidence, I am convinced that...

219
00:42:24,146 --> 00:42:29,586
...the blow that will defeat
Osman Bey won't come from the heathens...

220
00:42:29,586 --> 00:42:34,156
...but from the Kayı Tribe.

221
00:42:36,373 --> 00:42:41,623
I'll keep gathering information
until you come here.

222
00:43:11,385 --> 00:43:16,475
-Take it to my bey father.
-As you order, Malhun Hatun.

223
00:43:41,079 --> 00:43:45,079
What kind of trouble are you in,
Osman Bey?

224
00:43:45,277 --> 00:43:49,277
How will you get out of all these
troubles?

225
00:43:56,903 --> 00:44:00,903
The emperor called Nikola.

226
00:44:00,903 --> 00:44:05,203
-He will move out tomorrow.
-Will we raid him, Osman Bey?

227
00:44:05,203 --> 00:44:09,203
We can't stand idle, brother!

228
00:44:09,203 --> 00:44:13,203
We'll strike the heathens
in everywhere we see them!

229
00:44:17,378 --> 00:44:21,668
They'll be prepared.

230
00:44:21,668 --> 00:44:25,668
They will hide.

231
00:44:25,668 --> 00:44:29,898
They'll wait for us to set an ambush.

232
00:44:31,266 --> 00:44:35,846
But we'll strike them from where
they expect the least.

233
00:44:40,335 --> 00:44:45,815
-From here, it's all hills, Osman Bey.
-I know, brother.

234
00:44:45,815 --> 00:44:48,995
So, I'll send the alps on foot.

235
00:44:48,995 --> 00:44:51,425
Good idea.

236
00:44:51,931 --> 00:44:55,851
If you allow me, I want to lead them,
Osman Bey.

237
00:44:55,851 --> 00:44:59,411
You will stay here, brother.

238
00:45:01,506 --> 00:45:05,506
Osman Bey, it's your order, of course.

239
00:45:05,506 --> 00:45:09,506
But you choose me as the First Alp.
Do you regret that?

240
00:45:09,931 --> 00:45:14,681
When I'm on a campaign,
I'm the First Alp, brother.

241
00:45:15,501 --> 00:45:20,541
You'll stay in the tribe.
Here is also in danger.

242
00:45:23,085 --> 00:45:27,775
-Last time my nephew--
-Uncle!

243
00:45:29,250 --> 00:45:33,250
You'll stay here with my brother.

244
00:45:35,118 --> 00:45:39,578
And you won't leave here
no matter what.

245
00:45:39,578 --> 00:45:45,608
No one will enter our tribe without
my knowledge.

246
00:45:48,718 --> 00:45:52,718
As you order, Osman Bey.

247
00:45:55,889 --> 00:46:01,229
Uncle, you will obey whatever
my brother says.

248
00:46:18,670 --> 00:46:23,980
Bamsı Bey, what do you say?
How should we attack?

249
00:46:41,511 --> 00:46:46,711
If they know that we'll ambush,
they'll come crowded.

250
00:46:47,490 --> 00:46:51,490
There will be many martyrs.

251
00:46:51,490 --> 00:46:55,490
There will be many martyrs, Osman Bey.

252
00:46:55,849 --> 00:47:01,709
This will be as dangerous as it
taker longer.

253
00:47:11,030 --> 00:47:17,440
It will be a great jihad.
Everyone should get ready.

254
00:47:55,594 --> 00:47:59,814
So, tell me now.

255
00:47:59,814 --> 00:48:03,814
Should we take Göktuğ's head
for deceiving us...

256
00:48:03,814 --> 00:48:08,874
...or should we give him what he wants?
-The documents are real.

257
00:48:09,559 --> 00:48:14,169
-Does he have the rest of them?
-He says that he has it all.

258
00:48:16,485 --> 00:48:20,485
Do you think that we can trust
Göktuğ, Flatyos?

259
00:48:39,840 --> 00:48:43,840
I don't trust anyone for saving
my life once.

260
00:48:45,859 --> 00:48:50,889
But Göktuğ has no other choice.
I'm sure he'll take us to the documents.

261
00:48:54,270 --> 00:48:59,070
I will bring the gold.

262
00:49:17,688 --> 00:49:22,908
Osman will ambush Nikola.

263
00:49:24,344 --> 00:49:28,344
I will inform Süleyman about that.

264
00:49:29,111 --> 00:49:36,251
Osman will be ambushed
on his way to an ambush.

265
00:49:38,772 --> 00:49:43,652
Dündar Bey...
Dündar Bey...

266
00:49:45,170 --> 00:49:50,320
If Osman dies among all the alps...

267
00:49:50,320 --> 00:49:54,360
...no one will return.

268
00:49:54,360 --> 00:49:58,360
-So?
-So...

269
00:49:58,360 --> 00:50:03,440
...you want to be the bey but
tell me...

270
00:50:04,539 --> 00:50:11,079
If everyone dies, whose bey will you be?

271
00:50:14,497 --> 00:50:18,797
Do you think I'm a boy, woman?

272
00:50:19,943 --> 00:50:27,163
After I sit on the fur of the bey,
I'll think of that as well.

273
00:50:46,311 --> 00:50:50,311
Why are you stressed?

274
00:50:50,679 --> 00:50:56,269
My thumb ring is missing, woman.
I'm thinking about it.

275
00:50:58,334 --> 00:51:02,334
Maybe you dropped it while shooting?

276
00:51:15,549 --> 00:51:20,369
No, it was on my thumb then.

277
00:51:20,480 --> 00:51:24,670
It must've fallen when I was
going to Süleyman's shop.

278
00:51:24,670 --> 00:51:29,630
So, why don't you search for it
before anyone else finds it?

279
00:51:30,287 --> 00:51:34,287
I'll look when I'm going to Süleyman.

280
00:51:46,025 --> 00:51:52,595
Just another trouble. Who knows
how we'll save ourselves.

281
00:51:55,259 --> 00:52:00,609
Traders want markets.
Ghazis want jihad.

282
00:52:01,503 --> 00:52:08,683
A great conquest will have us
heard from everywhere.

283
00:52:09,745 --> 00:52:15,325
Then, the ghazis will join us.

284
00:52:16,101 --> 00:52:20,101
The path for new markets will
be opened.

285
00:52:20,101 --> 00:52:23,271
Traders will come.

286
00:52:23,846 --> 00:52:28,926
Osman is right, daughter.
If his heir will be a bey...

287
00:52:28,926 --> 00:52:33,186
...then, the mother should be
a bey's daughter.

288
00:52:33,955 --> 00:52:38,275
You are right, mother.
You are right.

289
00:52:39,358 --> 00:52:45,458
But a bey's daughter,
especially the one who'll give a heir...

290
00:52:45,724 --> 00:52:49,724
Will enter the tent and kick you...

291
00:52:49,724 --> 00:52:54,284
...out of the tent and Osman's
heart, you think.

292
00:53:00,018 --> 00:53:06,168
Don't worry. No one can replace you.

293
00:53:06,168 --> 00:53:09,468
Neither from this tent
nor from Osman's heart.

294
00:53:14,422 --> 00:53:16,912
A great conquest.

295
00:53:18,307 --> 00:53:22,307
We need a great victory.

296
00:53:27,367 --> 00:53:31,367
May I enter, Osman Bey?

297
00:53:36,657 --> 00:53:40,267
Come.

298
00:53:48,723 --> 00:53:52,323
What's wrong, Malhun Hatun?

299
00:54:05,646 --> 00:54:09,816
Where will we settle in, Osman Bey?
Tell me.

300
00:54:13,876 --> 00:54:19,516
So, you want to hear it as soon
as possible.

301
00:54:19,516 --> 00:54:22,506
Is there a need to wait?

302
00:54:25,827 --> 00:54:31,737
The home I want to give you is
around Bolu.

303
00:54:34,558 --> 00:54:40,558
-Why there?
-Big lands, big grasslands.

304
00:54:40,558 --> 00:54:47,258
Counsel with Umur Bey. If he thinks
it's appropriate, settle there.

305
00:54:47,768 --> 00:54:51,348
That can't be.

306
00:54:55,858 --> 00:55:01,568
I learned about these lands before
I came. We can't trade there.

307
00:55:03,042 --> 00:55:07,822
We don't only want to be shepherds
but traders too.

308
00:55:08,850 --> 00:55:13,990
Show us such a place that we'll be close
to trade centers.

309
00:55:17,830 --> 00:55:23,350
So, you learned about our lands?

310
00:55:25,926 --> 00:55:31,506
-So, you want to trade?
-The hand that gives is superior.

311
00:55:31,707 --> 00:55:37,327
Give, so that you'll be superior.
Give, so that we'll stand with you.

312
00:55:37,327 --> 00:55:42,317
And crush your enemies.
Be your shield against the traitors.

313
00:55:49,401 --> 00:55:53,401
Think about that, Osman Bey.

314
00:55:58,931 --> 00:56:02,461
Malhun Hatun!

315
00:56:06,149 --> 00:56:09,529
Wait.

316
00:56:24,427 --> 00:56:28,427
Umur Bey raised you well.

317
00:56:29,415 --> 00:56:36,265
If you had accepted that land,
you would lose my favor.

318
00:57:01,329 --> 00:57:07,199
These lands are your new home.

319
00:57:11,310 --> 00:57:15,310
May it be good.

320
00:57:15,310 --> 00:57:19,310
Dündar Bey will help you.

321
00:57:21,260 --> 00:57:25,710
Tell me if you need anything.

322
00:57:27,103 --> 00:57:30,383
You won't regret it, Osman Bey.

323
00:57:50,604 --> 00:57:54,214
A bey's daughter.

324
00:58:16,800 --> 00:58:20,570
May I enter, Osman Bey.

325
00:58:21,548 --> 00:58:24,878
Come, aunt.

326
00:58:27,415 --> 00:58:31,885
You wanted to see me.
You have things to say.

327
00:58:31,885 --> 00:58:35,885
Aunt...
My dear aunt...

328
00:58:36,279 --> 00:58:41,899
-I wish one thing from you.
-Not wish, your words are my orders.

329
00:58:41,899 --> 00:58:45,899
Not at all, aunt.

330
00:58:45,899 --> 00:58:49,179
Not at all.

331
00:58:49,897 --> 00:58:53,257
Tell me, Osman Bey.

332
00:58:53,360 --> 00:58:57,360
Your tribe is also invited, aunt.

333
00:58:57,899 --> 00:59:02,669
I want you to leave us with your
longing.

334
00:59:03,357 --> 00:59:10,847
Go, go and bring your tribe here.

335
00:59:13,743 --> 00:59:18,593
-You mean my siblings, huh?
-Yes.

336
00:59:18,781 --> 00:59:23,841
It's been so long.
I miss them.

337
00:59:25,121 --> 00:59:31,481
Convince them to come to
these lands, aunt.

338
00:59:33,312 --> 00:59:37,312
Send them my regards.

339
00:59:37,312 --> 00:59:41,672
And tell them that Osman Bey
is inviting them.

340
00:59:41,980 --> 00:59:46,830
Of course, I will, son.
But tell me.

341
00:59:46,904 --> 00:59:50,904
How will I bear this longing?

342
01:00:06,861 --> 01:00:10,861
Make way!

343
01:00:14,276 --> 01:00:18,276
With the name of Allah.

344
01:00:20,511 --> 01:00:27,381
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

345
01:00:51,339 --> 01:00:55,339
Dündar Bey is here too.

346
01:00:55,339 --> 01:00:58,689
I wanted to be blessed with
your words, my sheikh.

347
01:00:58,689 --> 01:01:03,339
Not at all.
Not at all.

348
01:01:06,446 --> 01:01:10,446
With the name of Allah.

349
01:01:31,370 --> 01:01:35,490
Longing is better than a reunion,
my friends.

350
01:01:35,490 --> 01:01:39,490
But it's still good to
reunite.

351
01:01:40,783 --> 01:01:46,083
We reunited with our loved one
and returned, thank Allah.

352
01:01:47,560 --> 01:01:51,560
We missed him again already.

353
01:01:51,560 --> 01:01:57,820
Tell me, my friends.
How are you?

354
01:01:57,820 --> 01:02:01,350
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah.

355
01:02:03,930 --> 01:02:10,430
Türker Hasan how is your business
in Söğüt?

356
01:02:10,651 --> 01:02:16,531
-Thank Allah, my sheikh
-Thank Allah, of course.

357
01:02:16,531 --> 01:02:22,871
We should be thankful for what
we have and what we don't have.

358
01:02:23,486 --> 01:02:28,266
For the good and the bad.

359
01:02:28,266 --> 01:02:33,046
It will increase with thankfulness
and decrease with complaints.

360
01:02:33,046 --> 01:02:38,696
Don't say it's little, it will be little.
Say it's a lot, it will be a lot.

361
01:02:41,001 --> 01:02:45,721
If people stop being grateful
in a country...

362
01:02:45,721 --> 01:02:49,721
...they won't have prosperity.

363
01:02:49,721 --> 01:02:54,651
We saw that Söğüt market
is in prospertiy. Mashallah.

364
01:02:55,556 --> 01:03:02,446
Tell me now, how are your
relations with non-muslim neighbors?

365
01:03:02,446 --> 01:03:06,446
We are good.
We are good.

366
01:03:06,446 --> 01:03:11,196
Mercy is worse than treason.

367
01:03:15,198 --> 01:03:19,768
How can a cruel man show mercy?

368
01:03:20,157 --> 01:03:25,687
Of course, there can be, my sheikh.
Mercy can take a man's faith.

369
01:03:26,148 --> 01:03:30,148
We missed this foresight, Kumral.

370
01:03:35,727 --> 01:03:41,347
We heard and learned from
Sage Tapduk.

371
01:03:41,574 --> 01:03:47,024
Let me tell you.
Who said that?

372
01:03:48,277 --> 01:03:52,277
Priest Odon.
Where did he say that?

373
01:03:52,811 --> 01:03:57,741
Sultan Gıyaseddin's city, Antalya's
Elmalı.

374
01:03:59,885 --> 01:04:04,785
Do you know Elmalı? Had anyone been
there?

375
01:04:04,881 --> 01:04:08,211
We know, my bey.
We know.

376
01:04:08,211 --> 01:04:13,051
It's not our place to talk about battles
when Dündar Bey is here.

377
01:04:13,207 --> 01:04:17,207
Not at all, my sheikh.
Not at all.

378
01:04:20,112 --> 01:04:26,152
When İmameddin Zengi of Mosul...

379
01:04:27,040 --> 01:04:33,200
...took Urfo from heathen Joselin...

380
01:04:33,200 --> 01:04:39,660
...European heathens came together
and started a campaign.

381
01:04:41,081 --> 01:04:47,556
Glorious Sultan Mesut wasn't going to
let the heathens succeed...

382
01:04:47,556 --> 01:04:53,746
...so he took all the way through
Anatolia.

383
01:04:54,331 --> 01:04:59,291
He broke one arm of the crusader
army in Eskişehir...

384
01:04:59,588 --> 01:05:04,458
...and the other part wanted to
pass the Toros mountains.

385
01:05:05,700 --> 01:05:09,680
They came...

386
01:05:09,680 --> 01:05:14,300
...they set camp at Toros
mountains.

387
01:05:15,107 --> 01:05:21,837
Crusaders had hundreds of thousands
of soldiers.

388
01:05:23,904 --> 01:05:28,854
So, what do that many
soldiers need?

389
01:05:29,710 --> 01:05:36,180
Heathens get hungry too. They need
food, water...

390
01:05:36,881 --> 01:05:41,831
True. In time...

391
01:05:42,111 --> 01:05:46,771
...the crusaders were left without
any food.

392
01:05:46,771 --> 01:05:51,351
They will seize the food of
the people.

393
01:05:52,076 --> 01:05:56,076
And 3 out of 4 houses...

394
01:05:56,076 --> 01:06:00,076
...are made of Rum families.

395
01:06:00,076 --> 01:06:05,756
So, the Rum people that they
embraced...

396
01:06:05,756 --> 01:06:12,521
...ran to the Turks of Elmalı
to save their food.

397
01:06:12,977 --> 01:06:19,847
They even fought with the heathens
in the ranks of the Turks.

398
01:06:21,547 --> 01:06:26,647
Crusaders finally surendered.

399
01:06:26,960 --> 01:06:34,330
The legends say that 3000 of them
asked for mercy.

400
01:06:35,354 --> 01:06:39,984
A Muslim can't hit the one
who ask for mercy.

401
01:06:39,984 --> 01:06:43,984
So, 3000 crusaders...

402
01:06:43,984 --> 01:06:47,984
...converts to Islam and settles
in Elmalı.

403
01:06:51,006 --> 01:06:59,146
That's why the priest said that.

404
01:06:59,724 --> 01:07:05,654
Mercy is worse than treason.

405
01:07:06,960 --> 01:07:10,960
Mercy to humans, mercy to animals...
From an ant to an elephant; mercy!

406
01:07:11,393 --> 01:07:22,616
The flag of the Kayı
is the flag of Islam.

407
01:07:31,256 --> 01:07:36,536
You came here with nothing but
swords and you conquered here.

408
01:07:41,057 --> 01:07:46,637
Swords take lands but...

409
01:07:46,924 --> 01:07:51,814
...to settle in that lands...

410
01:07:51,925 --> 01:07:56,125
...you should mercy to...

411
01:07:56,125 --> 01:08:00,635
...everything on these lands.

412
01:08:03,205 --> 01:08:08,835
Those who don't have mercy,
can't have faith.

413
01:08:11,190 --> 01:08:16,450
That's it, my friends.
That's enough for now.

414
01:08:16,450 --> 01:08:20,450
-I shouldn't take your time.
-Not at all.

415
01:09:59,157 --> 01:10:01,957
Mother!

416
01:10:27,458 --> 01:10:31,458
Bayhoca? I'm here, son.

417
01:10:34,089 --> 01:10:38,269
-Mother? Did I call you?
-You wandered about me.

418
01:10:41,846 --> 01:10:46,166
I had a dream, mother.
I'm fine.

419
01:10:46,409 --> 01:10:50,409
-Was it a nightmare?
-No, mother. I'm fine.

420
01:10:53,150 --> 01:10:57,950
You are sweating.
Tell me what did you see.

421
01:10:57,950 --> 01:11:03,050
-It's not bad, mother. Don't worry.
-Good then...

422
01:11:03,050 --> 01:11:07,050
...tell me if it's good.

423
01:11:12,059 --> 01:11:16,059
It was a pure white place.

424
01:11:16,897 --> 01:11:22,977
-Like a house?
-I don't know. It was white.

425
01:11:25,262 --> 01:11:29,262
A bird got out of my mouth.

426
01:11:29,263 --> 01:11:34,173
It flew away.

427
01:11:34,982 --> 01:11:38,982
It became invisible.

428
01:11:41,792 --> 01:11:46,372
It was like it was flying
away from a cage.

429
01:11:48,772 --> 01:11:53,212
-What kind of a bird was it?
-What kind, mother?

430
01:11:53,212 --> 01:11:56,612
A dream bird of course.

431
01:12:02,148 --> 01:12:08,528
Mother, you look sleepless.
I will sleep if you allow me.

432
01:12:09,206 --> 01:12:12,176
Sleep, son.

433
01:14:07,959 --> 01:14:12,919
It seems that you have news for me,
Dündar 'Bey'.

434
01:14:22,172 --> 01:14:26,172
I can't wait to hear it.

435
01:14:26,172 --> 01:14:30,172
What's that good news?

436
01:14:59,038 --> 01:15:03,898
You are lucky.
The documents are real.

437
01:15:04,977 --> 01:15:08,547
Did you doubt it.

438
01:15:09,571 --> 01:15:17,291
I owe you my life. But as
you can understand, Nikola had doubts.

439
01:15:17,547 --> 01:15:22,227
He freed him of his doubts?

440
01:15:22,227 --> 01:15:27,417
You'll find out when you meet him
for the gold. You are free now.

441
01:15:27,895 --> 01:15:30,005
Flatyos.

442
01:15:32,802 --> 01:15:37,620
There are no more doubts,
no more treason.

443
01:15:37,620 --> 01:15:42,660
There will be gold for my service.

444
01:15:44,084 --> 01:15:49,884
Göktuğ, Nikola's friendship is
much more valuable than gold.

445
01:15:50,381 --> 01:15:53,541
You will see that.

446
01:15:57,041 --> 01:16:00,641
I don't doubt that.

447
01:16:16,641 --> 01:16:22,541
-My bey, if Nikola gets these...
-He will, Göktuğ. He will.

448
01:16:24,990 --> 01:16:28,990
You will give them to Nikola.

449
01:16:29,142 --> 01:16:33,142
-I will?
-You will.

450
01:16:33,353 --> 01:16:37,353
You will give these unimportant
documents to Nikola.

451
01:16:38,443 --> 01:16:42,443
So that we can find out who he
is allied to.

452
01:16:44,160 --> 01:16:48,460
All right, my bey.
All right.

453
01:17:05,571 --> 01:17:09,571
Aunt.

454
01:17:11,247 --> 01:17:16,237
Bey of the Kayı, may Allah
give you health.

455
01:17:17,160 --> 01:17:22,440
Aunt, you are the post of this
tribe.

456
01:17:22,776 --> 01:17:28,046
Kayı women learned how to be
woman from you.

457
01:17:28,046 --> 01:17:34,006
It's time. Remind Kayı beys how to
be a bey.

458
01:17:35,086 --> 01:17:39,736
I'm grateful.
I'm thankful, aunt.

459
01:17:39,736 --> 01:17:46,096
Osman, you deserved the fur,
I defended that right.

460
01:17:48,054 --> 01:17:53,434
I saw you as the bey,
inshallah I'll see your state as well.

461
01:17:53,616 --> 01:17:57,846
Inshallah, aunt.
Inshallah.

462
01:18:01,574 --> 01:18:05,574
Women want to say farewell too.

463
01:18:06,736 --> 01:18:10,736
Mashallah to my girls.

464
01:18:11,882 --> 01:18:15,882
You are like angels.

465
01:18:19,163 --> 01:18:26,343
May Allah destine you everything you want.
May you never have grief.

466
01:18:28,953 --> 01:18:35,043
You are leaving us motherless,
Mother Selcan. No grief, huh?

467
01:18:38,266 --> 01:18:42,266
-What other grief do we need?
-Daughter...

468
01:18:44,255 --> 01:18:48,255
My pretty daughter...
Bala...

469
01:19:09,010 --> 01:19:13,780
You are leaving me both motherless
and fatherless.

470
01:19:16,201 --> 01:19:20,481
-You were both my mother and my father.
-Daughter...

471
01:19:20,481 --> 01:19:24,481
...why are you talking like
I will not return?

472
01:19:27,294 --> 01:19:31,294
Promise me, mother.
Promise me that you'll return.

473
01:19:31,294 --> 01:19:35,294
Destiny. If it's in our destiny,
inshallah I will return.

474
01:19:46,936 --> 01:19:51,866
Aygül... Aygül...
Aygül...

475
01:20:00,915 --> 01:20:06,855
Mother, which words can describe
your efforts on me?

476
01:20:08,313 --> 01:20:13,983
-What gratefulness can answer you?
-What are you saying, daughter?

477
01:20:21,338 --> 01:20:26,568
I had darkness in my heart,
you were my light.

478
01:20:27,524 --> 01:20:32,644
I forgot what it meant to be a woman.
You taught me.

479
01:20:34,031 --> 01:20:39,001
You taught me to fight
and stand.

480
01:20:39,001 --> 01:20:43,521
You will burn my heart, my daughter.

481
01:20:45,458 --> 01:20:50,688
Aygül, you will take good
care of your son, will you?

482
01:20:51,698 --> 01:20:56,598
You will teach what I taught you.

483
01:20:56,598 --> 01:21:00,598
From now, you have my place.

484
01:21:01,129 --> 01:21:05,129
Thank Allah,
Bala has Osman...

485
01:21:08,192 --> 01:21:12,842
...Gonca has Boran.

486
01:21:12,842 --> 01:21:16,842
You will marry again,
build a home.

487
01:21:29,592 --> 01:21:33,592
-Come on.
-Selcan Hatun.

488
01:21:40,159 --> 01:21:43,509
Forgive me.

489
01:21:45,480 --> 01:21:49,480
Forgiveness is for Allah, daughter.

490
01:21:49,480 --> 01:21:54,540
I understand you and know your heart.

491
01:21:57,170 --> 01:22:02,720
-Give me your blessing.
-It's yours.

492
01:22:14,640 --> 01:22:20,000
Now is the time to leave.
Take care of each other.

493
01:22:22,487 --> 01:22:26,487
Son, it's time to leave.

494
01:22:29,408 --> 01:22:33,408
Godspeed.

495
01:24:38,801 --> 01:24:43,951
Alps! Here...

496
01:24:45,141 --> 01:24:51,291
...is where the war begins.
Now...

497
01:24:52,425 --> 01:24:57,745
...you all will be alone with
your weapons.

498
01:24:59,613 --> 01:25:07,543
May Allah give you strength
and courage!

499
01:25:08,326 --> 01:25:13,696
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

500
01:25:18,974 --> 01:25:26,184
Now, when we leave the battlefield
victorious...

501
01:25:28,593 --> 01:25:34,203
...your shouts will tremble the sky!
-Amin!

502
01:25:38,578 --> 01:25:46,508
Now, we'll continue on foot
from here.

503
01:25:47,399 --> 01:25:53,759
We'll set our traps on the road
and set ambushes.

504
01:25:55,149 --> 01:25:59,149
-May Allah bless our efforts!
-Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!

505
01:26:45,166 --> 01:26:50,716
What a good day, isn't it?
Helen?

506
01:26:50,716 --> 01:26:54,496
It's good to see you happy, Nikola.

507
01:26:55,434 --> 01:26:59,844
I thought you would be stressed on
your way to Constantinople.

508
01:26:59,844 --> 01:27:06,404
If I wasn't taking a good present to
the emperor, I would be.

509
01:27:07,074 --> 01:27:14,024
-What's that good present?
-That secret is for me, Helen.

510
01:27:17,728 --> 01:27:23,188
Nikola, I'm grateful that you took
me with you.

511
01:27:27,598 --> 01:27:31,838
Holy Lord, this is very exciting.

512
01:27:31,838 --> 01:27:35,838
How could I keep you out
of this joy?

513
01:27:35,838 --> 01:27:39,838
I feel like this will be a lot
more fun I think.

514
01:27:40,477 --> 01:27:45,707
I will tell you on the way.
I'm very excited, Helen.

515
01:28:14,012 --> 01:28:19,662
Bring it, daughter.
Bring it. May Allah bless your hands.

516
01:28:25,098 --> 01:28:29,098
With the name of Allah.

517
01:28:29,399 --> 01:28:35,719
What's up, Hazal? You are so happy.
Is it because Selcan Hatun left?

518
01:28:38,530 --> 01:28:42,530
Lena. Lena!

519
01:28:42,530 --> 01:28:48,760
Stop it now. Aren't you happy
because Selcan Hatun left?

520
01:28:48,760 --> 01:28:54,370
-Didn't she bother you a lot?
-Right.

521
01:28:54,585 --> 01:28:58,585
She didn't bother me enough.

522
01:29:01,457 --> 01:29:04,847
May I enter?

523
01:29:07,159 --> 01:29:10,509
Come.

524
01:29:13,986 --> 01:29:17,986
Come, daughter.
Come, come.

525
01:29:17,986 --> 01:29:22,996
-Drink our sherbet. Come.
-I have no time. I'm looking for Dündar Bey.

526
01:29:29,986 --> 01:29:33,986
What will you do with Dündar Bey?

527
01:29:33,986 --> 01:29:38,706
We want to accept Osman Bey's invite
and settle on the borders.

528
01:29:38,930 --> 01:29:43,550
He wanted Dündar Bey to take care
of our settling.

529
01:29:54,281 --> 01:30:00,601
Don't worry, daughter.
My husband won't leave you alone.

530
01:30:01,294 --> 01:30:05,294
I know, Hazal Hatun.
I know.

531
01:30:05,442 --> 01:30:09,442
But what I didn't know is...

532
01:30:09,492 --> 01:30:15,252
...that Osman Bey was that much
in trouble.

533
01:30:17,454 --> 01:30:22,894
There is nothing Osman Bey can't
get over, don't worry.

534
01:30:24,099 --> 01:30:29,669
True. But even a mountain can't
stand against treachery.

535
01:30:31,332 --> 01:30:35,332
A traitor was killed in front of
his eyes.

536
01:30:40,520 --> 01:30:44,520
If it wasn't for Allah, it could be him.

537
01:30:45,910 --> 01:30:54,140
Who knows, daughter. Maybe it was
Nikola, maybe it was the Mongols.

538
01:31:00,337 --> 01:31:05,027
Maybe it was someone from the tribe.

539
01:31:07,638 --> 01:31:14,418
I heard that both Savcı Bey and
Dündar Bey was in quarrel with him.

540
01:31:35,371 --> 01:31:40,081
What do you mean, Malhun Hatun?

541
01:31:47,067 --> 01:31:51,867
But thank Allah that it didn't
go any further.

542
01:31:53,016 --> 01:31:58,216
Ertuğrul Bey's blood knew how
to be together.

543
01:31:59,635 --> 01:32:05,845
You are right. Despite all that,
Osman Bey saved our son.

544
01:32:07,487 --> 01:32:12,147
He took him out of the
castle of the heathens.

545
01:32:14,482 --> 01:32:19,062
That's where the Kayı
get their strength.

546
01:32:19,158 --> 01:32:27,168
In difficult times, they know how
to stand together.

547
01:32:27,168 --> 01:32:30,008
Thank Allah.

548
01:32:35,044 --> 01:32:42,664
May Allah give Osman Bey
a long life.

549
01:32:43,576 --> 01:32:49,086
May Allah protect him.

550
01:32:49,212 --> 01:32:52,082
Amin.

551
01:32:53,096 --> 01:32:58,796
Whatever the truth is, it will be
revealed. Sooner or later.

552
01:33:03,927 --> 01:33:08,697
It will. Of course.

553
01:33:13,153 --> 01:33:17,983
Dündar Bey is at Söğüt, my pretty girl.

554
01:33:19,671 --> 01:33:25,601
I should leave, then. We'll have plenty
of time to drink sherbet.

555
01:33:27,922 --> 01:33:31,922
Of course, we will have.

556
01:33:34,831 --> 01:33:39,821
-If you allow me.
-Of course.

557
01:33:59,920 --> 01:34:05,910
That girl. What is she going after?

558
01:34:07,147 --> 01:34:11,147
What is she trying to do?

559
01:34:13,177 --> 01:34:17,177
The truth.

560
01:34:38,374 --> 01:34:41,854
My bey, our alps are positioned
on that hill.

561
01:34:41,854 --> 01:34:45,304
-Have the archers positioned?
-They have, my bey.

562
01:34:50,217 --> 01:34:56,617
-We positioned the rocks as you ordered.
-No one will move without an order.

563
01:35:03,454 --> 01:35:07,454
-Brother.
-Brother.

564
01:35:22,284 --> 01:35:28,004
You were like him when you were young.
Always competing with the older ones.

565
01:35:30,738 --> 01:35:34,738
We learned courage from our older
brothers.

566
01:35:55,105 --> 01:35:59,105
Be careful, my son.

567
01:36:02,880 --> 01:36:09,060
Don't put yourself or your father
in danger.

568
01:36:09,499 --> 01:36:14,779
Don't worry, mother. We'll strike
the heathens and return safe and sound.

569
01:36:21,321 --> 01:36:25,321
Don't worry, my wife.

570
01:36:25,321 --> 01:36:29,731
He is a Kayı bey. He goes to
live his destiny.

571
01:36:30,380 --> 01:36:34,380
We are destined with jihad.
You know it.

572
01:36:34,380 --> 01:36:41,170
And our son prefers to fight with a sword
and not be a shepherd.

573
01:36:51,410 --> 01:36:55,410
You should get used to it.

574
01:37:18,511 --> 01:37:21,571
Come on, son.

575
01:38:01,105 --> 01:38:06,365
Bayhoca is a worthy Kayı bey.

576
01:38:07,767 --> 01:38:11,767
I missed my son's childhood, Osman Bey.

577
01:38:12,463 --> 01:38:17,583
He was in madrasahs,
he was getting education.

578
01:38:17,583 --> 01:38:21,893
Now, he has a sword in one hand
and a pencil on the other.

579
01:38:21,893 --> 01:38:29,283
We had enough of longing.
Now I won't keep him away from me.

580
01:38:37,828 --> 01:38:43,738
Osman Bey, I'm grateful that you
took me to this jihad.

581
01:38:43,738 --> 01:38:46,398
Thank you.

582
01:38:49,217 --> 01:38:53,217
We had to take you.

583
01:38:56,987 --> 01:39:02,797
If we hadn't, you would follow us.

584
01:39:04,975 --> 01:39:09,735
Come on. Don't bow your head.

585
01:39:09,920 --> 01:39:13,920
A Kayı bey stands straight.

586
01:39:14,141 --> 01:39:17,751
You are our future, Bayhoca.

587
01:39:17,751 --> 01:39:23,131
It's not about joining the jihad but
not listening to your bey.

588
01:39:27,979 --> 01:39:31,729
It won't happen again, my bey.

589
01:39:33,653 --> 01:39:40,863
I'll fight alongside my brave father,
and my bey uncle. I can die now.

590
01:39:42,369 --> 01:39:47,069
Return to the alps now.

591
01:39:54,429 --> 01:39:59,339
We'll swing swords in many more
battles, inshallah.

592
01:40:03,407 --> 01:40:04,987
Inshallah, brother.

593
01:40:08,049 --> 01:40:09,499
Inshallah.

594
01:41:15,825 --> 01:41:18,685
I'm hungry again.

595
01:41:20,573 --> 01:41:22,623
- You're hungry? Again?
- Huh.

596
01:41:43,624 --> 01:41:44,764
Eat it.

597
01:41:47,255 --> 01:41:51,305
You'll fight.
You have to be strong.

598
01:41:58,000 --> 01:42:00,070
What about you?

599
01:42:02,515 --> 01:42:05,695
I won't let people be hungry.

600
01:42:06,340 --> 01:42:08,470
- Even...
- Even?

601
01:42:17,833 --> 01:42:19,373
You.

602
01:42:30,656 --> 01:42:32,686
Take it, mad girl.

603
01:42:35,208 --> 01:42:36,858
You should eat.

604
01:42:37,200 --> 01:42:39,500
I'm not hungry.

605
01:43:16,116 --> 01:43:17,656
It's a sign.

606
01:43:49,037 --> 01:43:50,687
Nikola is coming.

607
01:43:52,397 --> 01:43:54,907
- Let's tell them
- Come on.

608
01:44:13,097 --> 01:44:16,337
- May it be easy.
- Thank you.

609
01:44:18,464 --> 01:44:20,294
Thank you.

610
01:44:27,713 --> 01:44:29,753
Thank you.

611
01:44:31,581 --> 01:44:32,951
My Gonca.

612
01:44:34,439 --> 01:44:37,469
What you're thinking
makes you happy, I guess.

613
01:44:37,741 --> 01:44:40,141
What is going on with you?

614
01:44:41,468 --> 01:44:43,598
What am I thinking?

615
01:44:44,974 --> 01:44:47,314
Boran Alp.

616
01:44:48,160 --> 01:44:51,000
Don't you think about marrying him...

617
01:44:51,000 --> 01:44:54,080
when he comes back?

618
01:44:54,366 --> 01:44:55,876
Bala.

619
01:45:30,407 --> 01:45:32,567
May it be easy, Hatuns.

620
01:45:36,343 --> 01:45:38,463
Thank you.

621
01:45:41,783 --> 01:45:43,723
If you're here to help...

622
01:45:44,971 --> 01:45:46,551
take it.

623
01:45:55,454 --> 01:45:59,454
Hatun of Bey saturates people.

624
01:45:59,701 --> 01:46:01,801
We hold swords.

625
01:46:06,769 --> 01:46:09,409
I wonder who is the killer of the potter.

626
01:46:10,033 --> 01:46:12,283
Did your Alps find any trace?

627
01:46:12,816 --> 01:46:14,726
They will, Hatun.

628
01:46:16,869 --> 01:46:18,969
Sooner or later.

629
01:46:23,467 --> 01:46:26,227
Are you waiting for another death?

630
01:46:26,893 --> 01:46:29,923
Why are you so concerned?

631
01:46:32,833 --> 01:46:35,553
Don't you have work
with Dündar Bey anyway?

632
01:46:36,617 --> 01:46:39,977
Mashallah, you hear everything.

633
01:46:42,562 --> 01:46:44,502
Hatun of Bey...

634
01:46:45,826 --> 01:46:50,846
stands with her Bey, not his behind.

635
01:46:51,578 --> 01:46:55,798
If he stands with him, she'll know what
happens in her tent.

636
01:46:57,486 --> 01:46:59,726
So that you're a Hatun of Bey...

637
01:47:01,371 --> 01:47:04,201
then listen to me well.

638
01:47:04,593 --> 01:47:08,313
My tent is ready for Osman Bey.

639
01:47:08,791 --> 01:47:12,311
Osman Bey's enemies may
become our enemies one day.

640
01:47:15,782 --> 01:47:18,422
I'm the daughter of a Bey, Bala Hatun.

641
01:47:19,205 --> 01:47:22,695
My tent's safety comes first.

642
01:47:22,831 --> 01:47:24,741
Then go to your tent.

643
01:47:26,972 --> 01:47:29,402
Don't make Dündar Bey wait.

644
01:47:45,787 --> 01:47:47,347
May it be easy.

645
01:47:48,704 --> 01:47:50,684
If you excuse me.

646
01:48:10,076 --> 01:48:11,236
Bala.

647
01:48:18,716 --> 01:48:21,646
Something's wrong with her.

648
01:48:22,145 --> 01:48:25,605
She is always in troubling situations.

649
01:48:26,745 --> 01:48:30,345
She'll go anyway.

650
01:48:32,972 --> 01:48:37,282
Until then, we'll keep an eye on her.

651
01:49:05,851 --> 01:49:07,041
My Bey.

652
01:49:11,657 --> 01:49:12,997
Tell me.

653
01:49:13,287 --> 01:49:15,277
We have a sign from the watchmen.

654
01:49:15,379 --> 01:49:19,379
Nikola and his soldiers are close.

655
01:49:23,948 --> 01:49:27,078
Do we have...

656
01:49:27,649 --> 01:49:30,039
equal soldiers?

657
01:49:31,369 --> 01:49:32,819
Yes.

658
01:49:42,779 --> 01:49:44,329
My Alps.

659
01:49:47,167 --> 01:49:48,397
My valiants.

660
01:49:52,552 --> 01:49:54,452
As Bamsı Bey said...

661
01:49:55,858 --> 01:49:58,558
if this keeps any longer...

662
01:49:59,040 --> 01:50:01,580
this will be more dangerous.

663
01:50:02,460 --> 01:50:06,290
So, we should kill Nikola...

664
01:50:07,536 --> 01:50:10,036
and leave here immediately.

665
01:50:16,198 --> 01:50:17,638
I know...

666
01:50:19,117 --> 01:50:20,797
we'll have martyrs.

667
01:50:22,224 --> 01:50:23,524
I know...

668
01:50:24,228 --> 01:50:25,598
we'll die.

669
01:50:28,613 --> 01:50:30,213
However...

670
01:50:30,503 --> 01:50:34,213
we won't let our sanjak down.

671
01:50:34,244 --> 01:50:36,754
Yes, my Bey!

672
01:50:42,628 --> 01:50:44,258
Come on.

673
01:51:29,076 --> 01:51:34,096
It's like I have seen Osman Bey's
condition.

674
01:51:34,710 --> 01:51:38,950
My brave daughter.

675
01:51:39,474 --> 01:51:41,604
My light.

676
01:51:42,010 --> 01:51:45,070
My special child...

677
01:51:45,390 --> 01:51:48,100
who doesn't let me feel the absence
of my martyr children.

678
01:51:48,118 --> 01:51:49,888
My Malhun.

679
01:51:50,965 --> 01:51:53,325
What are you thinking...

680
01:51:53,471 --> 01:51:55,111
about what she wrote?

681
01:51:55,421 --> 01:51:57,061
She says he has many enemies.

682
01:51:57,672 --> 01:52:00,052
He has few friends.

683
01:52:00,433 --> 01:52:03,223
Osman Bey has so many unbelievers around.

684
01:52:03,266 --> 01:52:05,596
All around him is Byzantine.

685
01:52:05,676 --> 01:52:09,876
He can't go any land.
He won't take lands from Germiyanids.

686
01:52:25,209 --> 01:52:29,259
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

687
01:52:38,930 --> 01:52:42,930
A Beylic is ancestral.

688
01:52:43,682 --> 01:52:46,342
It's not eternal.

689
01:52:47,034 --> 01:52:51,034
His grandfather Suleyman Shah...

690
01:52:51,841 --> 01:52:54,141
came from Aleppo yesterday.

691
01:52:56,019 --> 01:53:01,359
We've fought for Seljuqs for many years.

692
01:53:02,726 --> 01:53:08,556
What we have is that
everyone has a part of it!

693
01:53:10,820 --> 01:53:17,460
Did Mongols come to share out Seljuqs'
property to those Beys, Bahadır Bey?

694
01:53:19,789 --> 01:53:23,789
Chobanids, Germiyanids and the others...

695
01:53:23,789 --> 01:53:28,769
all of them have their thrones.

696
01:53:29,647 --> 01:53:33,647
Some of them still...

697
01:53:34,114 --> 01:53:37,534
run away from Mongols.

698
01:53:40,175 --> 01:53:44,175
We can't count how many of his
soldiers that Geyhatu has killed.

699
01:53:44,805 --> 01:53:48,445
However, thank Allah that you're alive.

700
01:53:53,443 --> 01:53:57,803
My Bey. Sarıcahan is ready for
tomorrow's accommodation.

701
01:53:57,992 --> 01:54:01,022
Send two more men.
They should go in disguised.

702
01:54:01,132 --> 01:54:04,182
- They don't know others.
- Your command.

703
01:54:04,205 --> 01:54:05,235
My Bey.

704
01:54:08,827 --> 01:54:13,197
Is it even possible for Seljuqs' heritage that
even Kızılbeyoğulları hasn't received...

705
01:54:13,247 --> 01:54:17,157
to be received by Osman
Bey, son of Ertuğrul Ghazi?

706
01:54:21,306 --> 01:54:26,866
Either he will conquer Tekfur Castle and
he will found his state in Bitinya...

707
01:54:28,285 --> 01:54:32,755
or he'll give up on his Beyhood.

708
01:54:35,576 --> 01:54:39,576
Let's say we're in the lands
that Osman has shown us...

709
01:54:40,929 --> 01:54:43,839
what if Osman attacks?

710
01:54:44,439 --> 01:54:49,279
What if what you've said happens?
What happens to Bayandur Tribe then?

711
01:54:51,222 --> 01:54:56,152
Kızılbeyoğlu will be Umur Bey's.

712
01:54:59,199 --> 01:55:02,239
Aren't Kayı Tribe and...

713
01:55:03,106 --> 01:55:05,326
Bayandur Tribe together anyway?

714
01:55:05,492 --> 01:55:09,802
Isn't our sanjak is Turk, Bahadır Bey?

715
01:55:10,420 --> 01:55:13,180
- Yes.
- So...

716
01:55:14,107 --> 01:55:16,397
Let's say Osman got weak...

717
01:55:16,727 --> 01:55:18,997
and his sanjak is down...

718
01:55:19,055 --> 01:55:26,515
will we let Byzantine take what we have?

719
01:55:29,709 --> 01:55:31,799
However...

720
01:55:32,472 --> 01:55:34,792
we have seen.

721
01:55:35,028 --> 01:55:36,908
We know tradition.

722
01:55:39,072 --> 01:55:43,292
We care about Bayandur's peace.

723
01:55:45,252 --> 01:55:49,062
Who gives happiness is my Allah.

724
01:57:26,228 --> 01:57:28,228
Nikola.

725
01:58:04,717 --> 01:58:06,647
Wait for my sign.

726
01:59:34,309 --> 01:59:35,539
Come on.

727
01:59:36,916 --> 01:59:39,796
Attack!

728
01:59:47,429 --> 01:59:49,339
Get ready for the battle order!

729
01:59:52,617 --> 01:59:54,597
Protect Nikola!

730
02:00:02,390 --> 02:00:05,650
Allah is eternal!

731
02:00:13,608 --> 02:00:15,688
Protect Nikola!

732
02:00:18,164 --> 02:00:20,324
Attack!

733
02:00:22,166 --> 02:00:26,356
Allah is eternal!

734
02:00:54,498 --> 02:00:56,528
Come on, valiants.

735
02:02:56,050 --> 02:02:58,250
Bayhoca!

736
02:03:11,140 --> 02:03:12,830
Bayhoca! Alps!

737
02:03:12,830 --> 02:03:14,240
Son!

738
02:03:16,284 --> 02:03:17,804
Son!

739
02:03:20,652 --> 02:03:24,172
- Son!
- Bayhoca!

740
02:03:39,186 --> 02:03:41,146
Son!

741
02:03:59,451 --> 02:04:03,011
You'll be okay, son.
Brother!

742
02:04:04,654 --> 02:04:06,354
My son!

743
02:04:47,987 --> 02:04:51,867
You'll be fine. You'll be
fine, my valiant.

744
02:04:51,964 --> 02:04:55,164
Hold on, my son.

745
02:05:06,906 --> 02:05:08,126
My son.

746
02:06:10,218 --> 02:06:14,218
Dündar Bey, Aygül Hatun
left with Osman Bey.

747
02:06:15,168 --> 02:06:20,228
Yes. She is the leader of Bacıs.

748
02:06:35,158 --> 02:06:37,998
What, daughter?
Are you here to eat?

749
02:06:39,107 --> 02:06:41,477
I ate, Dündar Bey.
Thank you.

750
02:06:42,367 --> 02:06:45,927
I wanted to see Söğüt.

751
02:06:50,146 --> 02:06:54,246
- I have some questions.
- Tell me.

752
02:06:54,382 --> 02:06:55,992
What are they?

753
02:06:56,802 --> 02:07:01,032
Osman Bey said that you'll be
dealing with settlement. (lodging)

754
02:07:08,611 --> 02:07:12,231
We'll talk about it when
your father comes.

755
02:07:12,732 --> 02:07:15,452
Now, I have some work to do.

756
02:07:15,790 --> 02:07:17,760
Sit.

757
02:07:32,641 --> 02:07:36,091
There are some things to be done before
my father comes.

758
02:07:37,501 --> 02:07:40,461
My father trusts me.

759
02:07:42,752 --> 02:07:44,052
However...

760
02:07:45,640 --> 02:07:49,320
does Osman Bey trust his uncle?

761
02:07:53,693 --> 02:07:55,143
What...

762
02:07:59,035 --> 02:08:01,335
What are you saying?

763
02:08:02,628 --> 02:08:05,338
He doesn't go to war with you anymore.

764
02:08:05,435 --> 02:08:08,275
But you're powerful in wars.

765
02:08:12,072 --> 02:08:15,692
Yes, I am and...

766
02:08:16,422 --> 02:08:20,632
when Osman Bey wants me, I'll go to war.

767
02:08:23,261 --> 02:08:25,131
However...

768
02:08:25,831 --> 02:08:28,241
he has something else to do now.

769
02:08:30,028 --> 02:08:35,318
Osman Bey doesn't
need his old uncle anyway.

770
02:08:42,027 --> 02:08:48,537
May Allah make your respect
and loyalty for Osman Bey everlasting.

771
02:08:58,737 --> 02:09:01,597
Yes.

772
02:09:08,784 --> 02:09:12,784
Let's start with water wells that are
placed on where the tent will be.

773
02:09:18,020 --> 02:09:19,600
I'm listening.

774
02:09:20,132 --> 02:09:21,622
Tell me.

775
02:09:35,814 --> 02:09:39,124
Son!
Son...

776
02:10:02,261 --> 02:10:05,581
Osman knows you're going to Byzantine.

777
02:10:08,372 --> 02:10:10,752
How can he know?

778
02:10:10,898 --> 02:10:13,878
What matters is that he knows.

779
02:10:14,146 --> 02:10:16,666
He'll set a trap for you.

780
02:10:16,888 --> 02:10:19,948
It's not about it!

781
02:10:20,425 --> 02:10:25,525
- How can he know!
- Don't dare to attack me again.

782
02:10:27,083 --> 02:10:31,083
Petrus.
You're in my castle.

783
02:10:31,204 --> 02:10:34,824
We're friends, Nikola.

784
02:10:35,798 --> 02:10:38,578
Friends don't attack each other.

785
02:10:41,740 --> 02:10:43,890
Instead of being angry...

786
02:10:45,899 --> 02:10:49,129
think of how you'll capture Osman.

787
02:11:11,506 --> 02:11:13,196
How do...

788
02:11:14,759 --> 02:11:18,159
how do you know about...

789
02:11:18,911 --> 02:11:21,191
Osman's trap?

790
02:11:21,715 --> 02:11:23,245
Dündar Bey.

791
02:11:23,970 --> 02:11:26,160
He is in our pocket.

792
02:11:28,383 --> 02:11:31,463
- Dündar?
- Yes.

793
02:11:32,428 --> 02:11:34,998
He is in our pocket now.

794
02:12:01,811 --> 02:12:06,201
Hold on, son.
Hold on, my valiant. Hold on!

795
02:12:06,390 --> 02:12:08,150
Hold on!

796
02:12:10,571 --> 02:12:12,711
My brother!

797
02:12:46,224 --> 02:12:47,954
A real commander...

798
02:12:48,622 --> 02:12:52,912
sacrifices his name for many people!

799
02:13:15,421 --> 02:13:32,951
Please contact us for any inquiries
